      "styles": [],
      "categories": [],
      "physical_description": null,
      "summary": "&#039;A coat of mail formed of seven folds of horse skin, used by the Araucarian Indians on the west coast of South America, taken from the body of an Indian who was shot by a party of Chilian Indians, sent to disperse an incursion of the native tribes&#039;.\r\nSuit of leather &#039;armour&#039; made from seven layers of horse hide sewn together with leather thongs and painted; there is a small hole, possibly from a bullet.",
